	(footprint "panel-pcb:WS2815_PLCC6_5.0x5.0mm_P1.6mm"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "1ce9b8eb-7a35-45b5-a7ca-6622bdef3f89")
		(at 160.7 73.246182)
		(descr "WS2815B-V1, 6-pin PLCC6 5.0x5.0mm, 1.6mm pad pitch. Pad numbering corrected to match the WS2815 pin diagram (VCC=1, VDD=2, DO=3, DIN=4, GND=5, BIN=6) - see Worldsemi WS2815B-V1 V2.0 datasheet https://www.tme.eu/Document/56a796ed8480f117bfc4e5341d7d9a26/WS2815B-V1_V2.0_EN.pdf. Pin 1: Worldsemi V2.0 labels it 'NC (suspended)', but it is the internally-regulated ~5V logic rail (the part runs off 12V VDD); the 100nF to GND on pin 1 is an optional noise filter on that internal rail. NOT the same pin numbering as KiCad's stock LED_WS2812_PLCC6 footprint, which is for the different 6-pin WS2812 part (pin 1=DO, pin 4=NC).")
