		(at 207.3 80.3 90)
		(descr "LCK-TCF829D vertical all-THT USB-C 16P (LCSC C53184807). *** BEST-GUESS TEMPLATE built 2026-07-25 from the datasheet PCB-layout view -- VERIFY EVERY COORDINATE against the datasheet before use. *** WHAT IS CERTAIN: pad NAMES match the J1 symbol and the datasheet pin table, so the electrical net mapping is correct (A1/A12/B1/B12=GND, A4/A9/B4/B9=VBUS, A5=CC1, B5=CC2, A6/B6=D+, A7/B7=D-, A8=SBU1, B8=SBU2). X-columns are from the datasheet dimension chain (1.00/3.00/5.00/7.00 full-widths -> pins at +/-0.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5; posts at +/-4.225 from 8.45). WHAT TO VERIFY/ADJUST: (1) A/B row Y-spacing -- set to +/-1.43 here from the '2.86' vertical dim, but the datasheet layout looks STAGGERED, so A and B may be offset in X and/or at different Y than a clean 2-row; (2) whether B-row X is offset 0.5mm from A-row; (3) post Y position (+/-2.5 assumed); (4) hole sizes (signal Ø0.5, power Ø0.8, posts oval 1.3x1.8 read from '8-Ø0.50', '8-Ø0.80', '4-1.30/4-1.80'). *** The attached 3D model is a PLACEHOLDER (CMUCF661016C, a DIFFERENT USB-C part) for visual bulk only -- it is NOT the LCK-TCF829D geometry. Do not use it for fit/clearance decisions. ***")
